#!/bin/sh
# vy-verifier-tunnel: the forced command of the verifier host's two tunnel accounts (12-vy-verifier.conf), which holds a session
# open for its forwarding and runs nothing else (benchmarks/live_verifier/host.py).
#   - prover: the audited node's `ssh -L` to a run's port. It prints `listening PORT` once a run's verifier, auditor's, listens on
#     one of the run ports (an `ssh -L` takes the prover's connection before the verifier listens, and the prover's connect doesn't
#     retry a closed one), so the prover connects after that line, and it ends once none listens, so the tunnel ends with the run.
#   - challenger: vy-challenger-1's `ssh -R` of a session's port (benchmarks/live_challenger/serve.py), held until the session
#     ends it.
set -eu
case "$(id -un)" in
  prover)
    uid=$(id -u auditor)
    listening() {
      ss -Hltne | awk -v u=" uid:$uid " '$4 ~ /^127\.0\.0\.1:795[1-8]$/ && index($0, u) { sub(/.*:/, "", $4); print $4; exit }'
    }
    until [ -n "$(listening)" ]; do sleep 1; done
    echo "listening $(listening)"
    while [ -n "$(listening)" ]; do sleep 5; done
    ;;
  challenger) exec sleep 86400 ;;
  *) echo "vy-verifier-tunnel: not a tunnel account" >&2; exit 3 ;;
esac
